            "text": "The user asks in Chinese: \"用一句话说明快速排序的平均复杂度,并简单解释为什么。\" — \"In one sentence, state the average complexity of quicksort, and briefly explain why.\"\n\nSo I need to answer in Chinese, in one sentence (or with a brief explanation). The instruction says \"用一句话说明...并简单解释为什么\" — state the average complexity in one sentence, and briefly explain why. I should keep it concise. Ideally one sentence that includes both the complexity and the explanation.\n\nQuicksort average complexity: O(n log n). Explanation: each partition roughly halves the array into two halves, needing O(n) work per level, and on average there are O(log n) levels; expectation over random pivots gives n log n.\n\nOne sentence: \"快速排序的平均时间复杂度是 O(n log n),因为随机/平均情况下每次划分大致将数组分成两半,每层划分需要 O(n) 的比较代价,平均递归深度为 O(log n),两者相乘即为 O(n log n)。\"\n\nThat's a single sentence in Chinese (with commas). Good. Should I use LaTeX? The format could be plain text with O(n log n). Keep it short. The user asked for one sentence, so just one sentence. Maybe I can add a tiny follow-up but they asked for one sentence; I'll respect that."
